      "content": "Grief often feels like a crushing weight that steals your identity and purpose, leaving you unable to see who remains within yourself. This numbness is a necessary phase where the world slows down so you can finally grieve the life you used to build. There is no timeline for returning to who you were; instead, focus on finding small, gentle ways to care for your own body until the weight lifts.",
      "source": "target",
